entries.english:
Copies of various documents:
1) Bishopric of Würzburg enfeoffment letter for Hans von Rosenberg Jr., concerning 1/3 of the tithe at Burken, a portion at Bofsheim, a portion at Rosenberg Castle, and a portion at Esselbach, 1445;
2) Palatinate enfeoffment letter for Erasmus von Rosenberg concerning 1/4 at Rosenberg, the fortress and the forecourt, 1451;
3) Agreement between Electoral Mainz and Albrecht Christoph von Rosenberg regarding hunting and grazing on Hochstetter territory and in this region, March 28, 1596;
4) Agreement between Hans von Vinsterlohe of Lautenbach and Zaisolf von Rosenberg concerning the sheep drive to Dürrhof, March 20, 1559;
5) Purchase contract between Balthasar Kettel as seller, and Arnold von Rosenberg as buyer, concerning a portion of the village of Buch including the castle mound and a quarter of the court there (a Wertheim fief), 1491;
6) Agreement between Hans and Konrad von Rosenberg regarding the tavern at Bofsheim and the sheep drive at Bronnacker, 1479;
7) Agreement between Albrecht, Philipp, Jacob and Hanns Carius von Rosenberg concerning the sheep drive at Hohenstadt, Rosenberg and Hirschlanden, November 20, 1559;
8) Document of Michael von Rosenberg wherein he acknowledges having sold to Hanns Glatz 1/8 of the grain tithe at Hohenstadt and the farm at Rosenberg;
9) Purchase deed concerning 1/4 of the tithe at Sindolsheim which Ulrich von Rosenberg sold to Hanns Rüdt of Bödigheim at Eberstadt, 1437;
10) Purchase deed concerning 1/4 of the great tithe at Sindolsheim, and half of the small tithe, then also half of a quarter of the tithe at Mattelnheim, which tithes Heintz von Seckendorf sold to Conrad von Rosenberg;
11) Agreement between the von Rosenberg and von Rüdt families regarding hunting, cattle grazing and the tithe of Sindolsheim, November 16, 1585;
12) Judgment letter of the Würzburg feudal judge on behalf of the von Rosenberg family as heirs to fiefs against the von Wolfskeel family as heirs to ownership of Hans Eucharius von Rosenberg, concerning the separation of the fief from the ownership, December 23, 1579;
13) Settlement between the von Rosenberg and von Wolfskeel families regarding what was conducted upon granting the proprietary properties at Rosenberg, March 23, 1580;
14) Compromise between the feudal heirs and the ownership heir of Philipp Jacob von Rosenberg concerning the separation of the fief from the ownership, March 11, 1584;
15) Receipt of the Rosenberg proprietary heirs to Albrecht Christoph von Rosenberg for 3,000 guilders for proprietary properties at Rosenberg sold to the latter, September 1, 1595;
16) Purchase deed wherein the deceased daughters and ownership heirs of Conrad von Rosenberg sell to Albrecht Christoph von Rosenberg all properties and revenues that had fallen to them by inheritance and ownership outside Rosenberg for 1,200 guilders, enacted on the Feast of St. Peter 1596;
17) Antichretic pledge of the tithe at Seckach from Albrecht von Rüdt to Albrecht Christoph von Rosenberg for a loan of 1,667 thalers, February 22, 1628.
